   "Cross out pulpectomy with gutta-percha: the radicular pulp is healthy, so pulpectomy is unnecessary, and gutta-percha does not resorb with the primary root.",
   "Cross out extraction: the tooth is restorable with a healthy radicular pulp, and 7.5 holds space for the 6s until around age 11 or 12.",
